{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1523371229,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM4MDEyNTI4OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2404#issuecomment-380125289"},"message":"At a first glance, I tend to prefer U1. It keeps the additional maintenance effort away, while still being easily available for non-datalad developers of extensions. I don't find that particularly \"ugly\".","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1523422604,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM4MDMyNzIxMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2405#issuecomment-380327212"},"message":"So you are saying that only selectively importing a single command and building one parser is 5x slower than importing all of it and rendering all docs etc...\n\nThat is surprising, giving that we looked at the startup differences when these changes were made and then merged.\n\nExcept for `--help` none of these commands should actually need to consult or load any entrypoints, hence that isn't a likely source of slowdown.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1523451310,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM4MDQ0MTUwOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2405#issuecomment-380441508"},"message":"I don't know yet \"the reason\" so saying nothing -- just presenting an observation with possible pointers to culprits","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1523495894,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM4MDY0NDA3MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2405#issuecomment-380644070"},"message":"as I've feared (and inquired at some point) and http://datalad.github.io/datalad/#core.startup.time_help_np somewhat pointed out, here I think is the main reason for slow downs:\n\n```shell\n$\u003e time python -c 'from pkg_resources import iter_entry_points'\npython -c 'from pkg_resources import iter_entry_points'  0.38s user 0.06s system 99% cpu 0.445 total\n```\nwhich is used now in multiple places \n```\n$\u003e git grep iter_entry_points\ndatalad/api.py:    from pkg_resources import iter_entry_points\ndatalad/api.py:    for entry_point in iter_entry_points('datalad.extensions'):\ndatalad/cmdline/main.py:from pkg_resources import iter_entry_points\ndatalad/cmdline/main.py:    for ep in iter_entry_points('datalad.extensions'):\ndatalad/interface/test.py:            from pkg_resources import iter_entry_points\ndatalad/interface/test.py:            module.extend(ep.module_name for ep in iter_entry_points('datalad.tests'))\ndatalad/metadata/metadata.py:from pkg_resources import iter_entry_points\ndatalad/metadata/metadata.py:    extractors = {ep.name: ep for ep in iter_entry_points('datalad.metadata.extractors')}\n```\nincluding `setup_parser` and thus it now is invoked even when there is no real need in discovering any additional entry point, e.g. running `datalad install` or `datalad get path`.\n\nI think I found one more piece (again clicking at that benchmark steady growing curve): #2414 but not sure how much that one is contributing (locally asv run didn't show any benefit)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1523496958,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM4MDY0Njc5Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2405#issuecomment-380646796"},"message":"I think a viable approach would be to setup an initial parser to handle only common opts, parse using `parser.parse_known_args` and then analyze first unparsed one -- if among known `interface_groups` - get and import that one and establish a full argparser only for that command and (re)parse the command line. For `--help` would just need to build a full one I guess","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1528780232,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5NjQ2NzQyNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2405#issuecomment-396467425"},"message":"That was done AFAIK.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1528780232,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTY3NTQwMTY2Mg=="},"status":2}]}